# Lunar Dominion — Unity .gitignore
# Place this file in the project root, next to the Assets folder,
# BEFORE your first commit in GitHub Desktop.
#
# What this keeps OUT (generated / local / rebuildable):
#   Library, Temp, Logs, build outputs, Visual Studio files
# What this keeps IN (do NOT add these to this file):
#   Assets/ (including all .meta files — Unity needs those),
#   Packages/, ProjectSettings/
# .meta files must be tracked. Never ignore *.meta.

# Unity generated folders — Unity rebuilds these on open
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Aa]sset[Ss]tore[Tt]ools/

# Visual Studio / Rider generated files
.vs/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
.idea/
*.sln.docstates

# Android / iOS build outputs
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.app
.gradle/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# Local crash / profiling dumps
*.dmp

# Unity crash recovery / temp / Burst debug — generated, rebuildable
# (these show up as untracked noise in git status)
# Note: Burst and backup folders carry the project name as a prefix
# (e.g. "Lunar Dominion_BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip"), so match with *.
# _Recovery.meta is the .meta file for the _Recovery folder itself.
_Recovery/
_Recovery.meta
.utmp/
*_BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip/
*_BackUpThisFolder_ButDontShipItWithYourGame/

# ---- Local-only content (added 2026-11-20, terrain-transplant) ----
# These live on Patrick's machine only BY DESIGN (Asset Store EULA
# content, hand-copied Blender outputs, scratch scenes) and were
# flooding `git status` with ~200 untracked lines. Ignoring them
# changes nothing on disk and never untracks a tracked file — it
# only stops git from listing the untracked ones.

# Asset Store packages (local-only, see Open Issues item 15)
/Assets/Creepy_Cat/
/Assets/Creepy_Cat.meta
/Assets/Mech_Constructor_Heavy/
/Assets/Mech_Constructor_Heavy.meta
/Assets/TerrainSampleAssets/
/Assets/TerrainSampleAssets.meta

# Scratch scenes at the Assets root (kit tests, candidates)
/Assets/*.unity
/Assets/*.unity.meta

# Hand-copied binary assets: kit prefabs, Blender FBX/PNG outputs.
# (Files already tracked here stay tracked and still show edits.)
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Models/*.fbx
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Models/*.fbx.meta
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Models/*.png
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Models/*.png.meta
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Models/*.prefab
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Models/*.prefab.meta
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Textures/*.png
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Textures/*.png.meta
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Textures/*.webp
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Textures/*.webp.meta

# Blender folder: the .py scripts are tracked; their Unity .meta
# files and the generated preview PNGs are local noise.
/Assets/_Project/Models/Blender/*.py.meta
/Assets/_Project/Models/Blender/ExteriorTerrainNormal.png
/Assets/_Project/Models/Blender/ExteriorTerrainNormal.png.meta
/Assets/_Project/Models/Blender/normal_hillshade.png
/Assets/_Project/Models/Blender/normal_hillshade.png.meta

# Unity-generated, never committed in this repo's workflow
/ProjectSettings/TimelineSettings.asset

# Round 2 (2026-11-20): the remaining untracked classes — the
# Resources Audio/UI folders (binary/local) and the Scripts .meta
# files. Script .meta files were never committed in this repo's
# workflow (code arrives via text pushes without them); the files
# stay on disk untouched, this only stops listing them.
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Audio/
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Audio.meta
/Assets/_Project/Resources/UI/
/Assets/_Project/Resources/UI.meta
/Assets/_Project/Resources/Textures/s.meta
/Assets/_Project/Scripts/**/*.meta
